From 56e02e762fd2bb966105253d5878bb498830dedb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 08:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): third weave dispatcher arm, compile-clean
 skeleton
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

M2 step 3 (docs/android-port.md). Patch 0052 turned DisplayXRWeaveClient and the
GPU-side provider into platform dispatchers with Windows and macOS arms; this
adds the Android arm in the same shape, with no re-architecture.

displayxr_weave_client_android.{h,cc} mirrors the mac pair and is deliberately
inert: InitializeCoreAndroid() checks that the seam is present (an adopted
DXR_IPC_FD plus a dlopen-able libopenxr_loader.so) and stops. IsSupportedAndroid
returns false — the WebXR contract is authoritative on a succeeding
requestSession('inline-3d'), so claiming support we cannot deliver would only
fail later. SubmitBatchAndroid logs once and fails gracefully.

Nothing is linked on Android, and that is the point: the client library's
compiled-in u_git_tag has to match the running displayxr-service, which it does
automatically as long as the runtime .so comes out of the installed runtime
package via the Khronos loader. So the Android analogue of patch 0001 vendors the
LOADER only, never a runtime copy.

displayxr_weave_gpu_android.{h,cc} is not yet a viz::DisplayXRWeaveProvider
subclass — that interface is IS_WIN||IS_APPLE and its per-platform arm takes the
platform texture type. Widening it with WeaveCanvasAndroid(AHardwareBuffer*) is
M1 work, where ProduceOverlayForWeave() starts yielding AHardwareBuffers. The
header records what M1 must own: one SCANOUT-backed shared window-sized AHB
input, the two fences the missing acquire fence forces, PruneTarget, and the
first-submit-only woven handle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Lf6vUbdL59MqXMwJxB489
